<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Lufthansa promotes new Airbus model-agency.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa promotes new Airbus model-agency.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's flag air carrier Lufthansa on Friday promoted the first commercial flight to Belgrade of the Airbus A3 19, a recent addition to its fleet, the Yugoslav news agency Tanjug reported.</p>
<p>&quot;Regular Frankfurt-Belgrade flights with the A3 19 will begin next year,&quot; Tanjug quoted Manfred Fock, Lufthansa manager for Yugoslavia, as saying.</p>
<p>Lufthansa, which currently has two A3 19s, plans to expand its fleet with another 18 of the latest Airbus models by the end of 1997, Fock said, according to Tanjug. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
